msgstr ""

msgid "**Image Pre-Pull**   [start.yml](tasks/utils/prepull/start.yml) pulls the images the deploy of the host runs, as listed by the `update_pull_images` filter, that the host does not hold yet under the pinned reference ([pull.yml](tasks/utils/prepull/pull.yml)), three at a time in a background job right before the shared services load; with nothing missing no job starts. It runs when `STORAGE_CONSTRAINED` and `RESET` are false and the host is a stack host, so never on a swarm worker. [reap.yml](tasks/utils/prepull/reap.yml) collects the job before the E2E run, or at the start of the destructor on a host without a server stage, and prints the pulls that failed. A failed pull or the time limit of `SYS_SVC_CONTAINER_PREPULL_ASYNC_TIME` does not fail the deploy, and each app still pulls its images itself."
msgstr ""

