# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Magento (Adobe Commerce Open Source)** is a powerful, extensible e-commerce platform built with PHP. It supports multi-store setups, advanced catalog management, promotions, checkout flows, and a rich extension ecosystem."
msgstr "**Magento (المصدر المفتوح)** هو منصة للتجارة الإلكترونية قوية ومكثفة مبنية مع PHP. وهي تدعم إنشاءات من عدة مواضع، وإدارة متطورة للرسوم، والترقيات، وتدفقات الخروج، ونظام إيكولوجي ذي ثراء للتمديد."

msgid "**Mail to and from onion addresses.** The new *svc-net-tor-smtp* role accepts mail for *.onion* recipients and delivers it over Tor. The applications reach an onion mail provider too: 27 roles now resolve the provider's onion host inside their containers and skip STARTTLS towards it, since no certificate can exist for an onion name and Tor already encrypts the link. GitLab's test suite checks that a password reset mail actually arrives."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Mail-to-ticket:** When ``web-app-email`` is present, the ``helpdesk`` mailbox is auto-provisioned and Zammad polls it to create tickets from incoming mail."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Mail-to-ticket:** When `web-app-email` is present, the `helpdesk` mailbox is auto-provisioned and Zammad polls it to create tickets from incoming mail."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Mailbox seed:** under the ``mailbox`` email policy of ``web-app-keycloak``, ``svc-db-openldap`` installs the timer. Only once the deploy has applied the mailbox layout, which in a deploy with Keycloak happens after Keycloak accepted the realm’s policy, `tasks/mailbox.yml <./tasks/mailbox.yml>`__ writes the root-only ``mailbox.json`` under ``DIR_RBAC_SYNC``; under the ``external`` policy ``svc-db-openldap`` removes it. While it exists, each run without ``--only`` gives every account of the users OU that holds no ``mail`` the address ``<uid>@<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>`` and the class ``infinitoMailboxUser`` before the hooks read the members. An existing ``mail`` value is never changed. The address comes from the ``ldap_mailbox`` module the deploy’s mailbox layout uses. The run binds as ``LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA``; its password lives in ``mailbox.json``, never in argv, the log, ``config.json``, or the ``RBAC_SYNC_LDAP`` a host hook receives."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Mailbox seed:** under the `mailbox` email policy of `web-app-keycloak`, `svc-db-openldap` installs the timer. Only once the deploy has applied the mailbox layout, which in a deploy with Keycloak happens after Keycloak accepted the realm's policy, [tasks/mailbox.yml](./tasks/mailbox.yml) writes the root-only `mailbox.json` under `DIR_RBAC_SYNC`; under the `external` policy `svc-db-openldap` removes it. While it exists, each run without `--only` gives every account of the users OU that holds no `mail` the address `<uid>@<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>` and the class `infinitoMailboxUser` before the hooks read the members. An existing `mail` value is never changed. The address comes from the `ldap_mailbox` module the deploy's mailbox layout uses. The run binds as `LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA`; its password lives in `mailbox.json`, never in argv, the log, `config.json`, or the `RBAC_SYNC_LDAP` a host hook receives."
msgstr ""

# " (CLI) وأدوات تطبيقية على شبكة الإنترنت لإزالة المخابئ، وإدارة قاعدة
