msgid "**`privileged_control_plane` (24):** `svc-bkp-local-2-device`, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`, `svc-bkp-remote-2-local`, `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`, `svc-bkp-volume-2-local`, `svc-dns-unbound`, `svc-net-firewall`, `svc-net-tor`, `svc-net-tor-smtp`, `svc-net-wireguard`, `svc-opt-keyboard-color`, `svc-opt-ssd-hdd`, `svc-opt-swapfile`, `svc-prx-openresty`, `svc-registry-cache`, `svc-registry-docker`, `svc-runner`, `svc-storage-nfs-client`, `svc-storage-nfs-server`, `svc-swarm-manager`, `svc-swarm-node`, `svc-virt-kata`, `update`, `web-app-openbao`. These roles can recover secrets, alter routing or host state, run code, change deployment state, or reach storage/control-plane sockets; they require a separate audited operations gateway and human approval rather than general-purpose application MCP."
