msgstr ""

msgid "Under ``route: all`` the bridge is the only entry. Docker falls through to the next nameserver whenever dnsmasq answers SERVFAIL, which is exactly what it answers while Tor is down, so any second entry would be a clearnet fallback for every container."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` dnsmasq drops to `user=dnsmasq`, and the deploy requires that user. Upstream DNS for direct names is admitted only for the effective UID of the running dnsmasq, read from `/proc/<MainPID>/status`. The deploy refuses that UID when it is 0 or 65534 or when processes other than dnsmasq run as it, because the admission would cover them too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` nothing on the host resolves beside dnsmasq: `resolve` leaves the `hosts:` line of nsswitch.conf; systemd-resolved, where present, gets a drop-in with `DNS=127.0.0.1`, an empty `FallbackDNS=` and `Domains=~.`; resolv.conf loses the clearnet nameserver; the docker daemon gets the bridge as its only resolver, because Docker moves on to the next nameserver on the SERVFAIL dnsmasq answers while Tor is down; and the deploy refuses `server`, `resolv-file`, `servers-file` and `conf-file` lines in `/etc/dnsmasq.conf`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all` the forward chain ends in its own `drop` and jumps nowhere, so no rule returns into a chain without one. Both chains accept local IPv6, and the output chain accepts IPv6 neighbour discovery."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all`, outbound SMTP and any other non-TCP traffic to unlisted destinations is dropped; add the MX hosts to `direct.include` when the node needs them. Time sync works against the pre-filled servers and the names below them only, and Tor itself needs a correct clock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `all`, outbound SMTP is undeliverable unless the recipients' MX hosts are in `direct.include`; every other non-TCP protocol needs a direct entry as well. Time sync works against the pre-filled servers only, and Tor itself needs a correct clock."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `external`, the `email` claim carries Keycloak's `email` field, so the realm keeps unproven addresses out of tokens:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `lazy` and `task` the models live on a node-local bind mount, so a rebuild or a recreate finds what an earlier run already fetched. `build` is mounted without it, because a bind is never seeded from the image and would hide what the build baked."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `mailbox`, a user created at runtime (admin console, admin API, registration) gets its LDAP `mail` from the [RBAC sync timer](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/README.md), which runs every 15 minutes (`SYS_SCHEDULE_MAINTANANCE_RBAC_SYNC`). Until its next run the user has no `mailbox` attribute and no `email` claim. The timer sets `mail` only on entries that hold none."
msgstr ""

msgid "Under `mailbox`, the claim carries the platform-owned mailbox with `email_verified` hardcoded to `true`, and the realm keeps `verifyEmail: false`."
msgstr ""

