msgid "Upstream support for enforcing each app's own second factor, for the 22 roles that declare `login.method.2fa`. \"Switch today\" is where the role reads `login.method.2fa.enabled`. Discourse, ERPNext, EspoCRM, Gitea, GitLab, Joomla, Moodle, Nextcloud, Odoo, pgAdmin, pretix and Zammad render their enforcement setting from `login.method.2fa.enforced` (Gitea with the role default `false`, see the schema criteria). Matomo and Weblate default to `false` and only offer the second factor: Matomo's enforcement would cut off the deploy's own API calls, and Weblate enforces per team only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Upstream targets Cloudflare Workers only: the code reads its bindings from ``cloudflare:workers``, persists to two D1 databases, two KV namespaces and an R2 bucket, and fires its ingest cycle from a cron trigger. A Node adapter build is therefore not available without porting the code."
msgstr ""

msgid "Upstream targets Cloudflare Workers only: the code reads its bindings from `cloudflare:workers`, persists to two D1 databases, two KV namespaces and an R2 bucket, and fires its ingest cycle from a cron trigger. A Node adapter build is therefore not available without porting the code."
msgstr ""

