msgid "What a token leaves open belongs to the line it stands in: `priority` covers every remaining combination in one sweep, `whitelist` keeps the rotation and the row's position in the matrix. A pin the row cannot take aborts the matrix rather than dropping the row, because a dropped row would report a green run for a combination that never ran. Such a pin is `@swarm` on a role without its own stack, `+tor` on a variant that pins `services.tor.enabled` false, `+multi` on a role with `reachability.single_mode: true`, or any axis that fights the run's own `mode`, `network`, `distros`, `filesystem` or `architectures` input, or `:arm64` on a role whose `meta/services.yml` declares `architectures: [amd64]`."
