msgid "[x] Each candidate the inventory rejects (`web-app-kix`, `web-app-funkwhale`, `web-app-fusiondirectory`, `web-app-openclaw`, `web-app-akaunting`) is listed with the reason it does not trust a header, or is moved into the list once it does. (`web-app-kix` is rendered with the reason of its `# nocheck: header-trust` marker, `roles/web-app-kix/templates/kix-proxy.default.conf.j2:1`, by `utils/roles/header_trust.py:header_trust_exemptions`. `web-app-funkwhale` and `web-app-akaunting`, which no file names, stay as prose at `docs/contributing/design/iam/rbac.md:139-144`, and `test_header_trust_table_not_committed.py::test_the_hand_written_candidates_stay_undetected` fails once the scan finds one of them or the role does not exist, with its negative control `test_a_detected_role_listed_as_candidate_is_reported`. `web-app-fusiondirectory` moved into the rendered list: `tasks/01_ldap.yml:25` hands `FUSIONDIRECTORY_HTTP_HEADER_NAME` (`X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`, `vars/main.yml:15`) to `files/shell/ldap/bootstrap.sh`, which sets `LoginHTTPHeader` on it behind the `sso_proxy_secret` check. `web-app-openclaw` moved because its trusted-proxy login trusts `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`.)"
